# Recipe Popup & Icon Support

This plan refines the Recipe Creator by moving it to a dedicated popup dialog and adding visual icons for Minecraft materials.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The recipe editor will now open in a separate window (Dialog).
> Icons will be dynamically generated based on the item name, but I will provide a way for you to supply your own PNG files for a custom look.

## Proposed Changes

### UI Components

#### [NEW] [RecipeDialog.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/RecipeDialog.java)
- A modal dialog containing the 3x3 grid and item browser.
- **Icon Support**: Uses a custom renderer to show visual icons in the grid slots and the product preview.
- **Product Preview**: Shows the custom block/item being edited (using its current pixel art texture if available).

#### [MODIFY] [ModMakerApp.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/ModMakerApp.java)
- Replace embedded `RecipeGridPanel` with a **"Setup Crafting Recipe"** button in both the Block and Item tabs.
- Store a reference to the `Recipe` object for the current element.

#### [NEW] [IconSystem.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/IconSystem.java)
- A utility to generate/fetch icons.
- **Dynamic Generator**: Creates stylized 32x32 icons for Minecraft materials (e.g., grey cube for iron, yellow for gold, brown for planks) with short text labels.
- **Local Fallback**: Allows the app to look for `.png` files in a local assets directory.

### Visual Polish
- Update the 3x3 grid buttons to use dark backgrounds and "slot" styling common in Minecraft GUIs.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1.  Click the "Define Recipe" button in the Block Tab.
2.  Assign ingredients in the popup.
3.  Observe the visual icons in the grid.
4.  Save and confirm the recipe persists in the main app window (via a "Recipe Set" status label).
